OCWORLD 1
# Engine test content for GRAPH-AS-CLASS. Two placements naming the SAME class, AN_Orbiter (declared
# by Content/Scripts/IdleMotion.ocgraph's CLASS record), at two different starting points.
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES. AN_Orbiter's own graph seeds a "home" VAR from its own entity's position at
# OnStart, then orbits that remembered point every OnTick -- see IdleMotion.ocgraph's own header
# comment. Placing two instances at DIFFERENT positions is therefore, by itself, the proof that two
# instances of one graph class carry INDEPENDENT VAR state: if they shared one store, both would
# orbit whichever entity's OnStart ran last, and their positions would coincide (or run in lockstep
# offset by a fixed vector) rather than genuinely diverging around two separate centres.
NAME OrbitDemo

# `none` in the asset slot is never read: LevelInstance.cpp skips building a raw mesh/physics entity
# for any placement whose className is non-empty (see OcWorldPlacement::className's own comment), so
# the asset column is inert here -- present only because PLACE's grammar is positional and the class
# keyword rides in the trailing key=value-style token region, not the leading columns.
PLACE none 0 0 0 0 0 0 1 class AN_Orbiter
PLACE none 400 0 0 0 0 0 1 class AN_Orbiter
